IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tlca-dates`
IMPORT `tlca-rules`
IMPORT `tlca-seat`

-- Limitation Act 1974 (Tas), child abuse claims -- worked cases for the survivor's questions (tlca-seat.l4), the date
-- helpers (tlca-dates.l4) and the two DEONTIC rules (tlca-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the
-- deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated
-- facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the day`
`nd` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000
`adult born` MEANS `d` 1 1 1970

`injury` MEANS `damages for personal injury to the person who was abused`
`death` MEANS `damages under the Fatal Accidents Act 1934 for the death of the person who was abused`
`someone else` MEANS `damages for injury to someone other than the person who was abused`
`other action` MEANS `another kind of action`
`sexual` MEANS `sexual abuse`
`serious physical` MEANS `serious physical abuse`
`psych from it` MEANS `psychological abuse arising from sexual or serious physical abuse`
`not serious` MEANS `physical abuse that was not serious`
`psych alone` MEANS `psychological abuse alone, or neglect`
`minor` MEANS `I was a minor not in the custody of a capable parent`
`incapable` MEANS `I was incapable by mental disorder with no independent legal representative`

GIVEN `y` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The time limit`
`last` `y` MEANS `the last day to bring the action is` `y`

`no limit` MEANS `no limitation period: the action may be brought at any time (s 5B)`
`suspended` MEANS `no last day yet: the time is suspended and the suspension has not ended (s 26A)`
`barred 1975` MEANS `barred before 1975, and this Act does not revive it (s 39(1))`
`other Act` MEANS `another Act's time limit applies (s 38)`
`not answered` MEANS `not an action this encoding answers`

§§ `Helpers`

-- The s 5B question with the usual s 38 / s 39 answers (no other Act, not barred before 1975).
GIVEN `a` IS A `What the action is`, `k` IS A `What the abuse was`, `m` IS A BOOLEAN, `r` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`any time` `a` `k` `m` `r` MEANS `Can I sue at any time for abuse I suffered as a child` `a` `k` `m` `r` FALSE FALSE

-- The time limit with no spell, no extension, born 1970.
GIVEN `a` IS A `What the action is`, `k` IS A `What the abuse was`, `m` IS A BOOLEAN, `disc` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The time limit`
`plain limit` `a` `k` `m` `disc` MEANS
    `By when must I bring my abuse action` `a` `k` `m` TRUE FALSE FALSE `disc` FALSE FALSE `adult born` FALSE `minor` `nd` FALSE `nd`

-- The time limit with an extension asked for.
GIVEN `disc` IS A DATE, `before 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The time limit`
`extended limit` `disc` `before 2018` MEANS
    `By when must I bring my abuse action` `injury` `not serious` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `disc` TRUE `before 2018` `adult born` FALSE `minor` `nd` FALSE `nd`

-- The time limit for abuse outside s 5B, with one spell.
GIVEN `disc` IS A DATE, `born` IS A DATE, `why` IS A `Why the clock stopped`, `from` IS A DATE, `ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The time limit`
`spell limit` `disc` `born` `why` `from` `ended` `to` MEANS
    `By when must I bring my abuse action` `injury` `psych alone` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `disc` FALSE FALSE `born` TRUE `why` `from` `ended` `to`

-- In time, no spell, no extension.
GIVEN `a` IS A `What the action is`, `k` IS A `What the abuse was`, `other` IS A BOOLEAN, `barred` IS A BOOLEAN, `disc` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`in time` `a` `k` `other` `barred` `disc` `the day` MEANS
    `Can I still bring my abuse action on this day` `a` `k` TRUE TRUE `other` `barred` `disc` FALSE FALSE `adult born` FALSE `minor` `nd` FALSE `nd` `the day`

§§ `Dates`

-- "3 years commencing on" 10 March 2020: 10 March 2020 is the first day, 9 March 2023 the last (fork F1).
#ASSERT `the final day of` 3 `years commencing on` (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `d` 9 3 2023
-- From 29 February 2020: 2023 has no 29 February; the last day is 28 February 2023 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `the final day of` 3 `years commencing on` (`d` 29 2 2020) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2023
-- Born 29 February 2008: the 18th birthday is taken as 28 February 2026 (fork F4).
#ASSERT `the 18th birthday for birth on` (`d` 29 2 2008) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026

§§ `s 5B -- can I sue at any time`

-- Sexual abuse as a minor, damages for the survivor's own injury: s 5B(1)(a).
#ASSERT `any time` `injury` `sexual` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Serious physical abuse of a minor who later died of it; the family's Fatal Accidents Act action: s 5B(1)(b).
#ASSERT `any time` `death` `serious physical` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Psychological abuse arising from the sexual abuse: s 5B(2).
#ASSERT `any time` `injury` `psych from it` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Physical abuse that was not serious: outside the grant; s 5A governs (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `any time` `injury` `not serious` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Psychological abuse alone, or neglect: outside the grant (finding 2).
#ASSERT `any time` `injury` `psych alone` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Sexual abuse of an adult: outside the grant.
#ASSERT `any time` `injury` `sexual` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An injury neither arising from nor related to the abuse.
#ASSERT `any time` `injury` `sexual` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A parent's own injury (nervous shock) from learning of the abuse: s 5B speaks of injury to the person abused (finding 4).
#ASSERT `any time` `someone else` `sexual` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An action that is not for damages for injury or death.
#ASSERT `any time` `other action` `sexual` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 38: another Act sets the period; this Act does not apply.
#ASSERT `Can I sue at any time for abuse I suffered as a child` `injury` `sexual` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 39(1): already barred before 1 January 1975 under the old law; this Act does not enable it (fork F2, finding 1).
#ASSERT `Can I sue at any time for abuse I suffered as a child` `injury` `sexual` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Both: s 38 takes the action out of this Act first, so s 39(1) does not speak.
#ASSERT `Can I sue at any time for abuse I suffered as a child` `injury` `sexual` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 26A(4) -- is my time stopped now`

-- A minor in no parent's custody (in care, say).
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A minor in the custody of the parent who abused him or her: that parent is the intended defendant.
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A minor in the custody of a parent whom the abuser may influence not to sue: a close relationship.
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A minor in the custody of a parent who is under disability.
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A minor in the custody of a capable parent: not a relevant person.
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An adult incapable for 28 days or more with no legal representative.
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same with an independent representative.
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same with a representative the person sued may influence.
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An adult not incapable for 28 days.
#ASSERT `Is my time to sue stopped for now` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5A(5), s 38A(3) -- can a judge give me 6 years`

-- Accrued before 1 July 2018, discoverability 30 June 2015: more than 3 years before 1 July 2018 (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Can a judge give me 6 years to sue` TRUE (`d` 30 6 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Discoverability 1 July 2015: exactly 3 years before, not more.
#ASSERT `Can a judge give me 6 years to sue` TRUE (`d` 1 7 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Accrued after 1 July 2018: s 38A(3) does not apply.
#ASSERT `Can a judge give me 6 years to sue` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can a judge give me 6 years to sue` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2010) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `By when must I bring my abuse action`

-- s 5B: no limitation period, whatever the discoverability day.
#ASSERT `plain limit` `injury` `sexual` TRUE (`d` 1 1 1990) EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `plain limit` `death` `psych from it` TRUE (`d` 1 1 1990) EQUALS `no limit`
-- Physical abuse that was not serious; discoverability 10 March 2020: 3 years commencing on it, last day 9 March 2023.
#ASSERT `plain limit` `injury` `not serious` TRUE (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `last` (`d` 9 3 2023)
-- Discoverability 29 February 2020: last day 28 February 2023.
#ASSERT `plain limit` `injury` `psych alone` TRUE (`d` 29 2 2020) EQUALS `last` (`d` 28 2 2023)
-- Sexual abuse of an adult: s 5A, 3 years.
#ASSERT `plain limit` `injury` `sexual` FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `last` (`d` 9 3 2023)
-- A parent's own injury from the abuse of the child: s 5A, 3 years (finding 4).
#ASSERT `plain limit` `someone else` `sexual` TRUE (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `last` (`d` 9 3 2023)
-- An action not for damages for injury or death: not answered here.
#ASSERT `plain limit` `other action` `sexual` TRUE (`d` 10 3 2020) EQUALS `not answered`
-- s 38 and s 39(1).
#ASSERT `By when must I bring my abuse action` `injury` `sexual` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 1990) FALSE FALSE `adult born` FALSE `minor` `nd` FALSE `nd` EQUALS `other Act`
#ASSERT `By when must I bring my abuse action` `injury` `sexual` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 1960) FALSE TRUE `adult born` FALSE `minor` `nd` FALSE `nd` EQUALS `barred 1975`
-- Extended to 6 years, accrued after 1 July 2018, discoverability 1 March 2019: last day 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `extended limit` (`d` 1 3 2019) FALSE EQUALS `last` (`d` 28 2 2025)
-- Extended to 6 years, accrued before 1 July 2018, discoverability 1 July 2015: allowed; last day 30 June 2021.
#ASSERT `extended limit` (`d` 1 7 2015) TRUE EQUALS `last` (`d` 30 6 2021)
-- An extension recorded but forbidden by s 38A(3) (discoverability 1 June 2015): 3 years, last day 31 May 2018.
#ASSERT `extended limit` (`d` 1 6 2015) TRUE EQUALS `last` (`d` 31 5 2018)

§§ `By when -- the s 26A suspension`

-- Born 1 June 2010, neglected at home; discoverability 1 June 2015; never in a capable parent's custody from 1 June 2015
-- until 18. Ordinary last day 31 May 2018. The spell 1 June 2015 to 31 May 2028 (the day before the 18th birthday) is
-- 4,749 days (13 years and the 29 Februaries of 2016, 2020, 2024 and 2028). 31 May 2018 plus 4,749 days: 31 May 2031 is
-- 4,748 days on (13 years and 29 Februaries 2020, 2024, 2028), so 1 June 2031 (fork F5: the days are added).
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 6 2015) (`d` 1 6 2010) `minor` (`d` 1 6 2015) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `last` (`d` 1 6 2031)
-- The same with a spell that began before the date of discoverability: counted from that date; same answer.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 6 2015) (`d` 1 6 2010) `minor` (`d` 1 1 2014) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `last` (`d` 1 6 2031)
-- Born 1 January 2005; discoverability 1 January 2020; a spell of 31 days, 1 to 31 January 2020. 31 December 2022 plus
-- 31 days: 31 January 2023.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2005) `minor` (`d` 1 1 2020) TRUE (`d` 31 1 2020) EQUALS `last` (`d` 31 1 2023)
-- A spell that begins on the last day (31 December 2022), stated to run to 5 January 2023, is cut at the day before the
-- 18th birthday (1 January 2023): one day, so 1 January 2023.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2005) `minor` (`d` 31 12 2022) TRUE (`d` 5 1 2023) EQUALS `last` (`d` 1 1 2023)
-- A spell that begins the day after the last day does not count.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2005) `minor` (`d` 1 1 2023) TRUE (`d` 5 1 2023) EQUALS `last` (`d` 31 12 2022)
-- A spell wholly before the date of discoverability does not count.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2005) `minor` (`d` 1 1 2019) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2019) EQUALS `last` (`d` 31 12 2022)
-- A minor's spell from 1 January 2020 not stated to end: it ends on 31 December 2022, the day before the 18th birthday;
-- 1,096 days (2020 has 29 February). 31 December 2022 plus 1,096 days: 31 December 2025 (1,096 days on: 365 + 366 + 365).
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2005) `minor` (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `last` (`d` 31 12 2025)
-- An adult incapable 1 to 27 March 2020 (27 days): under 28, does not count.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) `adult born` `incapable` (`d` 1 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 27 3 2020) EQUALS `last` (`d` 31 12 2022)
-- Incapable 1 to 28 March 2020 (28 days): the whole 28 days are added; 28 January 2023.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) `adult born` `incapable` (`d` 1 3 2020) TRUE (`d` 28 3 2020) EQUALS `last` (`d` 28 1 2023)
-- Incapable from 1 March 2020, not ended: no last day yet.
#ASSERT `spell limit` (`d` 1 1 2020) `adult born` `incapable` (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `nd` EQUALS `suspended`

§§ `Can I still bring it on this day`

-- s 5B: any day.
#ASSERT `in time` `injury` `sexual` FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 1990) (`d` 1 1 2040) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not serious physical abuse, discoverability 10 March 2020: 9 March 2023 in time, 10 March 2023 not.
#ASSERT `in time` `injury` `not serious` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) (`d` 9 3 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `in time` `injury` `not serious` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) (`d` 10 3 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Brought before the date of discoverability: in time.
#ASSERT `in time` `injury` `not serious` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 3 2020) (`d` 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Barred before 1975 (s 39(1)).
#ASSERT `in time` `injury` `sexual` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 1960) (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another Act's period (s 38).
#ASSERT `in time` `injury` `sexual` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 1990) (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A suspension that has not ended.
#ASSERT `Can I still bring my abuse action on this day` `injury` `psych alone` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE FALSE `adult born` TRUE `incapable` (`d` 1 3 2020) FALSE `nd` (`d` 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The time bar itself: 5 days allowed; brought on day 5 kept, day 6 not.
#ASSERT `bringing it at` 5 `keeps` (`the plaintiff must bring the action within` 5)
#ASSERT (NOT (`bringing it at` 6 `keeps` (`the plaintiff must bring the action within` 5)))

§§ `s 5C(1) -- is it child abuse`

#ASSERT `Is it child abuse under s 5C` `sexual` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse under s 5C` `psych from it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An act lawful at the time (finding 5).
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse under s 5C` `serious physical` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Abuse of an adult.
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse under s 5C` `sexual` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse under s 5C` `not serious` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 5C -- can I reopen my settlement`

-- Settled 30 June 2018, the day before s 5B commenced, after the period had expired: may apply.
#ASSERT `Can I reopen my settlement` `sexual` TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 6 2018) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you may apply to a court to set the settlement aside; it will if that is in the interests of justice (s 5C(2), (3))`
-- Settled 1 July 2018: not before that day.
#ASSERT `Can I reopen my settlement` `sexual` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 7 2018) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 5C does not reach it: the claim was settled on or after 1 July 2018`
-- Settled in 2010 within time (finding 6).
#ASSERT `Can I reopen my settlement` `sexual` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 5C does not reach it: no limitation period had expired when the claim was settled`
-- Already set aside.
#ASSERT `Can I reopen my settlement` `serious physical` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the settlement is set aside: you may bring the action (s 5C(2)), with no limitation period if s 5B applies`
-- An accepted Redress Scheme offer: s 5C(8), whatever else.
#ASSERT `Can I reopen my settlement` `sexual` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 5C does not apply: the settlement was an offer of redress accepted under the National Redress Scheme (s 5C(8))`
#ASSERT `Can I reopen my settlement` `not serious` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2020) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 5C does not apply: the settlement was an offer of redress accepted under the National Redress Scheme (s 5C(8))`
-- Not child abuse as defined: an act lawful at the time; abuse that was not serious.
#ASSERT `Can I reopen my settlement` `serious physical` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 5C does not reach it: what happened is not child abuse as s 5C(1) defines it`
#ASSERT `Can I reopen my settlement` `not serious` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 5C does not reach it: what happened is not child abuse as s 5C(1) defines it`

§§ `s 5C(4) -- what becomes of the agreement`

`release` MEANS `another agreement relating to the settlement, such as a deed of release or a confidentiality agreement`

#ASSERT `What becomes of the agreement once the settlement is set aside` FALSE `the agreement that settled my claim` `only to the child abuse` EQUALS `it is not void under s 5C(4): no court has set the settlement aside`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the agreement once the settlement is set aside` TRUE `the agreement that settled my claim` `only to the child abuse` EQUALS `it is wholly void`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the agreement once the settlement is set aside` TRUE `the agreement that settled my claim` `partly to the child abuse` EQUALS `it is void to the extent it relates to the child abuse`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the agreement once the settlement is set aside` TRUE `release` `partly to the child abuse` EQUALS `it is void to the extent it relates to the child abuse`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the agreement once the settlement is set aside` TRUE `release` `not to the child abuse` EQUALS `it is not void under s 5C(4): it does not relate to the child abuse`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the agreement once the settlement is set aside` TRUE `a contract of insurance` `only to the child abuse` EQUALS `it is not void under s 5C(4): a contract of insurance is excepted`
#ASSERT `What becomes of the agreement once the settlement is set aside` TRUE `an agreement that does not relate to the settlement` `only to the child abuse` EQUALS `s 5C(4) does not reach an agreement that does not relate to the settlement`

§§ `s 5C(5) -- can the other party get back what it paid`

`void ground` MEANS `because the agreement is void under s 5C`
`other ground` MEANS `on some other ground`

-- The bar itself: seeking to recover on the void ground breaches it.
#ASSERT `seeking to recover breaks the s 5C(5) bar`
#ASSERT `Can the other party get back what it paid me` TRUE `the agreement that settled my claim` `only to the child abuse` `void ground` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the other party get back what it paid me` TRUE `release` `partly to the child abuse` `void ground` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Another ground: s 5C(5) does not speak (fork F9).
#ASSERT `Can the other party get back what it paid me` TRUE `the agreement that settled my claim` `only to the child abuse` `other ground` EQUALS NOTHING
-- No order: nothing is void, so s 5C(5) does not speak.
#ASSERT `Can the other party get back what it paid me` FALSE `the agreement that settled my claim` `only to the child abuse` `void ground` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A contract of insurance is not made void: s 5C(5) does not speak.
#ASSERT `Can the other party get back what it paid me` TRUE `a contract of insurance` `only to the child abuse` `void ground` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 5C(6), (7) -- how much of the earlier payment`

-- Solely about the abuse: all of it.
#ASSERT `How much of my earlier payment can the court take into account` 100000 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS 100000
-- Solely about the abuse, and a part stated as well: solely governs (fork F10).
#ASSERT `How much of my earlier payment can the court take into account` 100000 TRUE TRUE 30000 EQUALS 100000
-- Not solely; it expressly indicates 30,000 for the abuse.
#ASSERT `How much of my earlier payment can the court take into account` 100000 FALSE TRUE 30000 EQUALS 30000
-- Not solely and no indication: half of the total, 50,000.50 of 100,001.
#ASSERT `How much of my earlier payment can the court take into account` 100001 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS 50000.5
